    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Atmospheric blocking and climate change",
    "problem": "Predicting future changes in atmospheric blocking is challenging due to a lack of comprehensive theory and a pervasive underestimation of its occurrence by climate models, leading to low confidence in projections.",
    "method": "This paper proposes an approach for robust blocking analysis by using several different identification indices, considering results trustworthy only when they are consistently found across the multiple methods, thus overcoming the uncertainty from any single definition.",
    "task": "The task is to review the state of knowledge on atmospheric blocking under climate change, summarizing model performance, underlying dynamics, and projected future changes in the frequency and characteristics of blocking events and their associated impacts.",
